{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And He put a word in his mouth.</b> Now what is this 'putting'? And what does the verse lack by saying 'Return to Balak and thus shall you speak'? Rather, when he heard that he was not permitted to curse, he said: Why should I go back to Balak to distress him? So the Holy One, blessed be He, placed a bridle and hook in his mouth — like a man who guides a beast with a hook to lead it wherever he wishes. He said to him: Against your will you shall return to Balak (ibid.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:23.754345537Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}